schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "Setting Up to Receive Crypto: A Step-by-Step Guide"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A 5-step walkthrough for a nonprofit/organisation to start accepting
    crypto donations: choose a donation platform, verify nonprofit status,
    set up the account, connect a donate button/widget to the website, then
    test before going live. Also flags automatic tax-receipt generation and
    common setup mistakes.
  audience: nonprofit/organisation staff new to accepting crypto donations
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      Article frames setup as "about an hour," but the real bottleneck it
      names is gathering nonprofit verification documents, which is not
      within the org's direct control on that timeline.
  related_concepts: []
  related_resources:
    - the-giving-block
    - infinite-giving
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/setting-up-receive-crypto.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    Frontmatter lists source "CryptoAltruists Web3 Impact Toolkit" — this
    article appears to be a derivative/summary of that toolkit's content, not
    independently reported. assessed-but-excluded: no high-risk
    people/location/TEK/MRV content.
